  "description": "A crystallised pheromone trail on the Plains (data/terrain.ts `spire`): three shards grown out of the dirt, each faceted — the left face lit, the right in shade, a darker sliver on the far right and a pale catch of light down the lit edge, which is what says glass rather than paint. A smaller crystal buds off the big one's foot and chips of it lie at the base. The signal glows near the tip of the big shard, lit from inside, and lays a faint pink on the ground in rings: the hive's light, and the one part of a spire that shines. The cut spires at the camp (`ss.base.stump`) are this with the signal gone out of them. Shadow and footprint where the old document had them. Generated by scripts/terrain.py.",
